[36m(TaskRunner pid=190305)[0m [response] To solve this problem, we need to maximize the real part of the expression \((75 + 117i)z + \frac{96 + 144i}{z}\) where \(z\) is a complex number with \(|z| = 4\). Let's represent \(z\) in its polar form as \(z = 4e^{i\theta} = 4(\cos\theta + i\sin\theta)\).
[36m(TaskRunner pid=190305)[0m 
[36m(TaskRunner pid=190305)[0m First, we substitute \(z = 4(\cos\theta + i\sin\theta)\) into the expression:
[36m(TaskRunner pid=190305)[0m 
[36m(TaskRunner pid=190305)[0m \[
[36m(TaskRunner pid=190305)[0m (75 + 117i)z = (75 + 117i)4(\cos\theta + i\sin\theta) = 4(75\cos\theta + 75i\sin\theta + 117i\cos\theta - 117\sin\theta) = 4((75\cos\theta - 117\sin\theta) + i(75\sin\theta + 117\cos\theta)).
[36m(TaskRunner pid=190305)[0m \]
[36m(TaskRunner pid=190305)[0m 
[36m(TaskRunner pid=190305)[0m \[
[36m(TaskRunner pid=190305)[0m \frac{96 + 144i}{z} = \frac{96 + 144i}{4(\cos\theta + i\sin\theta)} = \frac{96 + 144i}{4} \cdot \frac{\cos\theta - i\sin\theta}{\cos^2\theta + \sin^2\theta} = (24 - 36i)(\cos\theta - i\sin\theta) = 24\cos\theta - 24i\sin\theta - 36i\cos\theta + 36\sin\theta = (24\cos\theta + 36\sin\theta) - i(24\sin\theta + 36\cos\theta).
[36m(TaskRunner pid=190305)[0m \]
[36m(TaskRunner pid=190305)[0m 
[36m(TaskRunner pid=190305)[0m Now, we add these two results together:
[36m(TaskRunner pid=190305)[0m 
[36m(TaskRunner pid=190305)[0m \[
[36m(TaskRunner pid=190305)[0m 4((75\cos\theta - 117\sin\theta) + i(75\sin\theta + 117\cos\theta)) + ((24\cos\theta + 36\sin\theta) - i(24\sin\theta + 36\cos\theta)) = (4(75\cos\theta - 117\sin\theta) + 24\cos\theta + 36\sin\theta) + i(4(75\sin\theta + 117\cos\theta) - 24\sin\theta - 36\cos\theta).
[36m(TaskRunner pid=190305)[0m \]
[36m(TaskRunner pid=190305)[0m 
[36m(TaskRunner pid=190305)[0m Simplifying the real and imaginary parts, we get:
[36m(TaskRunner pid=190305)[0m 
[36m(TaskRunner pid=190305)[0m \[
[36m(TaskRunner pid=190305)[0m 300\cos\theta - 468\sin\theta + 24\cos\theta + 36\sin\theta = 324\cos\theta - 432\sin\theta,
[36m(TaskRunner pid=190305)[0m \]
[36m(TaskRunner pid=190305)[0m \[
[36m(TaskRunner pid=190305)[0m 240\sin\theta + 468\cos\theta - 24\sin\theta - 36\cos\theta = 444\sin\theta + 432\cos\theta.
[36m(TaskRunner pid=190305)[0m \]
[36m(TaskRunner pid=190305)[0m 
[36m(TaskRunner pid=190305)[0m So the expression we want to maximize is:
[36m(TaskRunner pid=190305)[0m 
[36m(TaskRunner pid=190305)[0m \[
[36m(TaskRunner pid=190305)[0m 324\cos\theta - 432\sin\theta + i(444\sin\theta + 432\cos\theta).
[36m(TaskRunner pid=190305)[0m \]
[36m(TaskRunner pid=190305)[0m 
[36m(TaskRunner pid=190305)[0m The real part of this expression is \(324\cos\theta - 432\sin\theta\). To maximize this, we can use the method of Lagrange multipliers or recognize that this is a dot product of vectors. The maximum value of \(a\cos\theta - b\sin\theta\) is \(\sqrt{a^2 + b^2}\), where \(a = 324\) and \(b = 432\). So the maximum value is:
[36m(TaskRunner pid=190305)[0m 
[36m(TaskRunner pid=190305)[0m \[
[36m(TaskRunner pid=190305)[0m \sqrt{324^2 + 432^2} = \sqrt{104976 + 186624} = \sqrt{291600} = 540.
[36m(TaskRunner pid=190305)[0m \]
[36m(TaskRunner pid=190305)[0m 
[36m(TaskRunner pid=190305)[0m Thus, the largest possible real part of the given expression is \(\boxed{540}\).
