[36m(TaskRunner pid=190305)[0m [response] To solve the problem, we need to maximize the real part of the expression \((75 + 117i)z + \frac{96 + 144i}{z}\) where \(|z| = 4\). Let's represent \(z\) in polar form as \(z = 4e^{i\theta} = 4(\cos\theta + i\sin\theta)\).
[36m(TaskRunner pid=190305)[0m 
[36m(TaskRunner pid=190305)[0m First, we substitute \(z = 4e^{i\theta}\) into the expression:
[36m(TaskRunner pid=190305)[0m \[
[36m(TaskRunner pid=190305)[0m (75 + 117i)z = (75 + 117i)4(\cos\theta + i\sin\theta) = 4(75\cos\theta + 117i\cos\theta + 75i\sin\theta - 117\sin\theta) = 4(75\cos\theta - 117\sin\theta + i(117\cos\theta + 75\sin\theta)).
[36m(TaskRunner pid=190305)[0m \]
[36m(TaskRunner pid=190305)[0m \[
[36m(TaskRunner pid=190305)[0m \frac{96 + 144i}{z} = \frac{96 + 144i}{4e^{i\theta}} = \frac{96 + 144i}{4(\cos\theta + i\sin\theta)} = \frac{(96 + 144i)(\cos\theta - i\sin\theta)}{4(\cos^2\theta + \sin^2\theta)} = \frac{(96 + 144i)(\cos\theta - i\sin\theta)}{4} = 24(\cos\theta - i\sin\theta) + 36i(\cos\theta - i\sin\theta) = 24\cos\theta + 36\sin\theta + i(36\cos\theta - 24\sin\theta).
[36m(TaskRunner pid=190305)[0m \]
[36m(TaskRunner pid=190305)[0m Adding these two expressions together, we get:
[36m(TaskRunner pid=190305)[0m \[
